Facts needed and language to verify
Every [bracket] in this deck needs an answer from Ostra before launch. The brief leaves specialty, budget, brand assets, content ownership and the launch deadline open, so the copy is written to flex around them.
Facts needed from the client
[ ] Specialty and project types: new builds, remodels, extensions, anything else
[ ] City or regions served
[ ] Years in practice, number of homes built, team size
[ ] Whether the studio delivers the build or designs only
[ ] Typical budget ranges, and whether they can be published
[ ] Typical timelines for each stage
[ ] Three to six named projects with sizes, years, credits and photography rights
[ ] Client quotes with written permission
[ ] Awards, press and certifications, with proof
[ ] Registration number, insurance and professional memberships
[ ] Consultation format: length, price (free or paid), response time
[ ] Open roles, and whether Careers should launch at all
[ ] Who owns and approves content, and the launch deadline
Language to verify
• Customer language. The words here come from the brief, not from real clients. Check them against inquiry emails, call notes and reviews, and swap in the phrases clients actually use.
• "Custom homes". Confirm this matches how the studio describes its work and how clients search.
• "Free of obligation" and response times. Only publish what the team will honour.
• Sustainability claims. Publish only measured results or named certifications.
• Legal pages. Privacy, terms and cookies need legal review.
• Headline choice. Test the three hero options with real visitors before settling.